  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## AI DATA CENTER COMMUNITY SIMULATION — V2

A hypothetical, neutral STS classroom model with SDG 6 as its primary focus. No default is a measurement or forecast of actual PAX Silica infrastructure. Add the group members' names before submission.

## HOW TO USE

Select starting counts (1–50 each), then Setup / Reset. One visible house represents one household. Build More +1 adds one facility, capped at 50. Run / Pause advances months; Step Month advances exactly one 30-day month. Statistics opens a numerical summary. Sustainable Solutions enables one intervention at a time. Repeating it never stacks benefits. Setup clears history and interventions. Starting counts and all advanced assumptions are applied only at Setup.

Charts show elapsed years, with 12 months per year, from actual monthly outputs. The default run ends at 72 months and freezes until Setup. At 1366 × 768 hide the Command Center via Tabs → Command Center; scroll vertically for plots and assumptions. At 1920 × 1080 plots fit below the main scene. The native layout has a fixed width.

## EQUATIONS AND UNITS

IT energy = facilities × IT capacity (MW) × utilization × 720,000 kWh/month.
Site water = IT energy × WUE (L/IT kWh) / 1,000,000 ML.
Facility freshwater request = site water × (1 − reuse share).
Household request = households × liters/day × 30 / 1,000,000 ML.
Grid demand % = 100 × (facilities × IT capacity × utilization × PUE × (1 − solar share) + households × kW/1000) / grid capacity MW.
ML = million liters. PUE changes electricity; it does not enter the WUE equation.

The reservoir recharges before allocation, spilling any water above capacity. Allocation is proportional, community-first, or data-center-first. Available water cannot be negative. Unmet water demand is recorded without adding an invented shutdown mechanism. Grid demand can exceed 100%; that indicates modeled demand above capacity, not simulated blackouts.

## LAND, ARTWORK AND RECOVERY

Separate 50-entry slot lists location homes and facilities independently of turtle IDs. The river, roads, homes, and indicator sidebar are protected. Each facility occupies 3 × 3 patches and clears vegetation in its 5 × 5 construction area. Baseline vegetation is recorded after homes are placed and before facilities are built. Green coverage is current vegetation / baseline. Reforestation adds 1/12 of baseline vegetation per month on cleared, unoccupied eligible patches. New construction restarts recovery on its own cleared area. Trees appear as vegetation regrows; wildlife is a habitat illustration, not a population model. The river's changing width illustrates reservoir stock; its entire original channel remains protected.

## ILLUSTRATIVE WELL-BEING

The landscape artwork uses reproducible irregular tree groves, varied sizes and clearings. House slots are shuffled and slightly offset, with nine protected patches around each rounded center. Reset recreates the same layout. These presentation changes preserve resource calculations and vegetation totals. Preview or restore the original V2 layout from ../backups/2026-10-13-before-natural-layout/.

Score = 0.40 × water stock % + 0.30 × max(0, 100 − grid demand %) + 0.30 × green coverage %.
Healthy ≥75; Moderate ≥50 and <75; Stressed ≥25 and <50; Critical <25.
Weights and thresholds are teaching choices, not measured human health. High starting counts do not force a Healthy label. Allocation outcomes are reported separately; this score is not a measure of fairness.

## INTERVENTIONS AND LIMITS

Recycled water substitutes 50% of facility site water. Solar supplies 40% of facility electricity, with no direct water effect. Reforestation affects vegetation, with no change to recharge. Building and enabling solutions update prospective requests and indicators immediately, without withdrawing another month's water or recording a fake chart point. Last-month balances remain historical. No guaranteed recovery. Excludes CO₂, pollution, waste heat, e-waste, disease, jobs, costs, independent population health, and detailed hydrology.

## CREDITS AND REFERENCES

Artwork: [Icons8](https://icons8.com), Fluency family: Cottage, Server, Deciduous Tree, Deer, Recycling, Solar Panel. PNG assets are cached locally for offline classroom use as part of this model, not a standalone icon pack. [Attribution guidance](https://icons8.com/license).

[NetLogo 7.0.4 Bitmap extension](https://docs.netlogo.org/7.0.4/bitmap.html) is bundled with NetLogo.
[U.S. DOE FEMP: Cooling Water Efficiency Opportunities](https://www.energy.gov/cmei/femp/cooling-water-efficiency-opportunities-federal-data-centers) supplies metric background; all numerical defaults here are illustrative.

Legacy model, tests and results are preserved separately. V2 intentionally changes the scope and must not be presented as numerically equivalent to V1.]]></info>
